Faxbot: the T.38 gateway ends a fast modem signal the far end left open (spandsp 0.0.6).

Live over Telnyx on 6 October 2026, the first fax received over T.38 failed.
The carrier's T.38 carried a training check its own modem had cut short (7
packets instead of about 51), so the fax engine rightly refused it. Telnyx
then sent two trainings that ended at once, with no data. spandsp 0.0.6's
gateway never marks such data finished, so it played V.29 fill to the engine
for seconds at a time and did not listen to the engine meanwhile: the engine's
answer (failure to train, which makes the sender retrain at a lower speed)
never reached the sender, and the engine, waiting for silence, gave up (E100).
Replaying the captured T.38 packets into spandsp reproduces it: no answer
reaches the far end, with or without 0002; with this change it reaches the
far end 1.5 s after the training check, within the sender's 3 s wait. The
call that worked, the send-direction captures 0002 was proven with, and a
training check the engine sends are unchanged.

--- a/res/res_fax_spandsp.c
+++ b/res/res_fax_spandsp.c
@@ -165,6 +165,8 @@
